WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.893 --> 00:00:04.963
- [Violet] Sustainability is key.

00:00:04.963 --> 00:00:07.238
It's not meant to be a privilege.

00:00:07.238 --> 00:00:10.230
It's more than selling your
products in the market.

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:11.992
- [Andy] It's about being
good stewards of the planet

00:00:11.992 --> 00:00:14.220
that we live on and
protecting the resources

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:16.106
that are out there.

00:00:16.106 --> 00:00:17.601
- [Sydney] We can't just have a few people

00:00:17.601 --> 00:00:19.345
working on it and then other people saying,

00:00:19.345 --> 00:00:21.913
"Okay, they're working
on it, we don't have to."

00:00:21.913 --> 00:00:23.520
Everyone needs to work together.

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:25.137
- Whether you're just recycling at home,

00:00:25.137 --> 00:00:27.569
or watching how much water you're using,

00:00:27.569 --> 00:00:31.652
lots of little things can
add up to a big change.

00:00:37.554 --> 00:00:41.054
- Clean drinking water is quite important.

00:00:44.108 --> 00:00:48.124
Western Kenya is a very
rich area in times of rain,

00:00:48.124 --> 00:00:52.220
but unfortunately most of
this rain goes into rivers

00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:54.137
that are not protected.

00:00:55.695 --> 00:00:58.593
People wash their clothes
in the same water.

00:00:58.593 --> 00:01:00.640
They will take their animals to drink

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:03.130
water from those same rivers.

00:01:03.130 --> 00:01:05.219
By the time the people
at the bottom of the hill

00:01:05.219 --> 00:01:09.386
get access to that water,
it's quite contaminated.

00:01:11.714 --> 00:01:13.481
- At Method, water's one
of the main ingredients

00:01:13.481 --> 00:01:15.779
in our product, so we
look to develop techniques

00:01:15.779 --> 00:01:17.946
that can offset the usage.

00:01:19.736 --> 00:01:21.345
In the beginning we set a goal,

00:01:21.345 --> 00:01:23.470
for a lead platinum certification,

00:01:23.470 --> 00:01:26.456
to be an ecologically advanced factory.

00:01:26.456 --> 00:01:28.910
To reduce our carbon footprint,

00:01:28.910 --> 00:01:30.465
we've got the greenhouse on the roof.

00:01:30.465 --> 00:01:34.186
We look at sustainability from
how can we have our business

00:01:34.186 --> 00:01:37.242
and really minimize its
impact on the environment

00:01:37.242 --> 00:01:40.931
but also even be restorative
to the environment.

00:01:40.931 --> 00:01:43.239
- Styrofoam, actually,
when it gets to landfills,

00:01:43.239 --> 00:01:45.895
it takes a long time to decompose.

00:01:45.895 --> 00:01:48.630
The Eco-Bin was a robotics
team project at first.

00:01:48.630 --> 00:01:53.000
We decided to go talk to the
people at Friendship Village.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:55.703
They told us that styrofoam was one of

00:01:55.703 --> 00:01:57.623
their biggest problems.

00:01:57.623 --> 00:02:02.172
And so, we invented a way
to make non-toxic glue.

00:02:02.172 --> 00:02:05.879
We pour our solution of
delaminate and other chemicals

00:02:05.879 --> 00:02:10.046
onto it and we reduced
it to 1/20th of its size.

00:02:16.265 --> 00:02:18.099
- [Violet] It's very
easy to work with kids,

00:02:18.099 --> 00:02:20.415
because they are good agents of change.

00:02:20.415 --> 00:02:24.070
They will go back home and
teach their own parents.

00:02:24.070 --> 00:02:26.320
LifeStraw works through ultra-filtration.

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:29.350
It holds back all the microorganisms,

00:02:29.350 --> 00:02:31.842
and the clean water is sieved out.

00:02:31.842 --> 00:02:33.704
I love my job because it answers for me

00:02:33.704 --> 00:02:35.624
the question, "Why?"

00:02:35.624 --> 00:02:39.035
Seeing their faces when they
see the difference in the water

00:02:39.035 --> 00:02:40.618
is an honor for me.

00:02:43.027 --> 00:02:45.226
- [Andy] I've got a lot
of pride for being here.

00:02:45.226 --> 00:02:47.438
I started when there was
nothing on this site.

00:02:47.438 --> 00:02:49.653
We chose to be part of the local community

00:02:49.653 --> 00:02:51.432
and see how Method's investment

00:02:51.432 --> 00:02:54.773
could positively impact the
community that we reside in.

00:02:54.773 --> 00:02:57.644
- As kids it was always "Later on in life

00:02:57.644 --> 00:03:00.634
"we could have a big future."

00:03:00.634 --> 00:03:03.362
It turns out that you can
accomplish big things now,

00:03:03.362 --> 00:03:05.307
it doesn't have to be later on.

00:03:05.307 --> 00:03:06.209
- [Andy] It's rewarding.

00:03:06.209 --> 00:03:08.507
You're not just here to make soap.

00:03:08.507 --> 00:03:09.795
This is the only planet that we have

00:03:09.795 --> 00:03:11.887
so it's important for
us to take care of that

00:03:11.887 --> 00:03:15.387
and have it there for future generations.

